      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T07:34:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The map call triggered by `prepareForReturnToCache` has a special handling for error: it will call `setDeleteASAP`. Should we call `setDeleteASAP` after an error regardless of whether it\u0027s by `prepareForReturnToCache` or normal `asyncMap`?\n\nAlso do we really need a mutex for the `fAsyncMapCallbacks`? I don\u0027t know whether we really call `asyncMap` concurrently.",
